[break] the-engine-is-told-by-a-prefix
rule: The script engine is told in the dependency graph by its package's whole name.
file: xtask/src/checks.rs
in: reaches_engine
find: line.split_whitespace().next() == Some(ENGINE)
replace: line.starts_with(ENGINE)
caught-by:
    checks::tests::the_engine_is_found_in_the_listing_by_its_name

[break] ext-add-without-the-engine-says-something-else
rule: In a build without the script engine, `cineris ext add` says the build has no script engine.
file: crates/cineris-cli/src/ext.rs
in: no_script_engine
in-string: has no script engine
replace: has a script engine
caught-by:
    cineris-cli::bin/cineris ext::tests::ext_add_without_the_script_engine_says_the_build_has_none

# A build without the script engine runs the configuration's hook commands
# through the same seam as the build with it, and holds the gating hooks of
# each extension that stands approved, since nothing of it runs. The
# decision is built in every build, and its tests run in the ordinary one
# (`ext::without_engine`); only a build without the engine puts it in a
# session.

[break] an-approved-extensions-gate-lapses-without-the-engine
rule: In a build without the script engine, an extension that stands approved holds its gating hooks on their events, failing: its gates do not lapse because the build cannot run it.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/without_engine.rs
in: holding
find: holding.held.push(Held {
replace: drop(Held {
